{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/248846-justifications-for-raising-primal-urge","id":248846,"title":"Justifications for raising Primal Urge?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-04T07:49:37-07:00","id":248846,"title":"Justifications for raising Primal Urge?","content":"I struggle with raising the werewolf power stat and I was wondering if folks here had any tips or ideas on raising that pesky Primal Urge score and maybe making seem more worthwhile beyond that ability to spend more essence and going above human norms on attributes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T08:10:33-07:00","id":248875,"title":"","content":"Supernatural resistance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:03:39-07:00","id":248949,"title":"","content":"1e had a lot of problems getting people to invest in power stats, considering the massive price and that there was usually a drawback. Obviously, you can spend more energy per turn.<br /> <br /> Werewolf's attempt to alleviate this was the Aspects, from Signs of the Moon, granting you bonuses to play up your type when you reached 3, 7 and 10 Primal Urge.<br /> <br /> There's also some stories that aren't backed up by mechanics, like the story of Jericho Glass, who changed drastically upon reaching Primal Urge 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:16:26-07:00","id":248954,"title":"","content":"Idigam also ties your regeneration to Primal Urge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T10:26:07-07:00","id":248958,"title":"","content":"It is difficult to justify Primal Urge in 1e especially with Werewolf which uses the oldest system of scaling when it comes to essence use per level","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T11:08:11-07:00","id":248983,"title":"","content":"I'd just say that since the Werewolf state is a mystical one there are no hard rules for how a Werewolf will grow in power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T11:11:31-07:00","id":248986,"title":"","content":"1st Edition reasons - supernatural resistance, spend more Essence, more time in Gauru, Attribute and Skill maximums.<br /> <br /> My quick &amp; dirty hack was to halve the XP cost and adjust the Essence spending limit to match the 1:1 ratio that (most of) the other games that came after had. More Essence means more Gifts can be used at once, and more time in Gauru seemed to help a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T04:43:04-07:00","id":249694,"title":"","content":"Being werewolf? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But really. often changes to forms, exploring Shadow Realm, being more wolf like. Generally, playing the game itself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> If I remember, Primal Urge in 1ed also limit how many items you can change with - not only pants, but fetishes and/or weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T21:47:28-07:00","id":250484,"title":"","content":"I think he wants actual IC justifications for raising it, guys.<br /> <br /> Here are some:<br /> <br /> A developed understanding of the Shadow, it's denizens and perils, as expressed thru the lens of instinct, highlighted by the Occult Skill. Rites would come into play, as well.<br /> <br /> The Wolf Must Hunt. Survival is directly linked to how an Uratha shapeshifts. How many gifts have you infused your essence with? don't you feel your spirit side bulging like a trained muscle now and then?<br /> <br /> Intimidation is the only social skill not diminished by Primal Urge. Those gaining potency on it begin to use it as a matter of course among the Sheeps that compose the otherwise denominated Herd. How is your standing among the local Forsaken? Can you raise higher in the totem pole?<br /> <br /> There you have it: Mental, Physical and Social paths to increase your PU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 09-06-2014, 12:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T01:45:43-07:00","id":255905,"title":"","content":"holy shit new dots x8?! Jesus thats an exp sink... assuming your character even lives long enough to get high enough to be a legend in 1st ed... I really really really want to assume the new cost system is similar to requiems 2nd ed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T02:58:11-07:00","id":255924,"title":"","content":"I wish people would do interesting things like starting with higher powered characters more often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}